Wheel data model (category, file path) interface where category is ROOT
or data, platlib, purelib or maybe None or '' for the ROOT category.

file path is the path, without the prefix in wheel that labels its
category. <name>-<version>.data/platlib/<file path>

Move it to an inner tarfile that's as streaming as possible. Possible to
go data -> tar -> hasher -> zip writer to collect our RECORD hash. Or,
wheel archive automatically hashes all incoming data.

Collect all of the original wheel's dist-info probably in RAM? because
we can't write them while the streaming inner-tarfile is also open.

Then those zipinfo's get written into the new zip.

It's very possible that if we call the new file
`name-version.data.tar.zst` then an extracter might look for
name-version.data<category>

But it probably looks for *.data/<category>/files so the slash prevents
those kinds of problems...


Zip can write CRC etc. after file data instead of in local header, for less
seeks while writing. But then we have the problem of not knowing the compressed
size without consulting the compression format, or the central directory header
and the footer for the file.

# Write updated header info
if self._zinfo.flag_bits & _MASK_USE_DATA_DESCRIPTOR:
    # Write CRC and file sizes after the file data

See ZipInfo.FileHeader() for the header that goes before each file in the
archive, in addition to the file list at the end.
